data: {"seq":1,"turn_id":"task_1c203ca7d29e2a3014387ff320039e0f","type":"turn_created","ts":"2026-11-26T18:25:44.936659+08:00","data":{"deep_research":false,"text":"# Inventory summary misclassifies product labels\n\nA daily import sometimes contains labels such as `\" TEA \"` or `\"Pens\"`.\nThey should aggregate into the same groups as `\"tea\"` and `\"pens\"`. Read\n`records.py` and the catalogue contract in `catalog.py`, then update\n`records.py`. Preserve the catalogue mapping, fallback group, and quantities.\n\nThe contents of repo/ are already staged at the workspace root. The tool path for the target is exactly records.py. Use read_file on records.py first, write your change to records.py, then run a public smoke test with exec_shell.","turn_index":0},"internal":{"source":"host","type":"task_created","task_seq":1,"payload":{"text":"# Inventory summary misclassifies product labels\n\nA daily import sometimes contains labels such as `\" TEA \"` or `\"Pens\"`.\nThey should aggregate into the same groups as `\"tea\"` and `\"pens\"`. Read\n`records.py` and the catalogue contract in `catalog.py`, then update\n`records.py`. Preserve the catalogue mapping, fallback group, and quantities.\n\nThe contents of repo/ are already staged at the workspace root. The tool path for the target is exactly records.py. Use read_file on records.py first, write your change to records.py, then run a public smoke test with exec_shell.","turn_index":0,"deep_research":false}}}

